            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GodivaGirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had several bags of fresh berries frozen that my family picked this summer. Instead of buying store bought jam I decided to give this a try. I thawed out the berries and used in place of fresh. This was very easy and good! I will continue to use this recipe and not buy store bought jam anymore!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe helped me use up some less-than-delicious strawberries (i.e. flavorless). I wasn't looking for sugar free, so I chopped up my strawberries, added sugar and water to them and let them simmer until they fell apart. Then I added in the Jello (I used raspberry flavored) and followed the recipe from there. I also added in some lemon juice, which I really think added a nice extra bit of flavor. I would definitely use this recipe again as a way to use up any extra fruit! Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2018-03-04T01:01:44.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Merline"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't like the idea of adding artificial strawberry flavoring with the Jello, so substituted an envelope of unflavored Knox gelatin and 1 cup erythritol (My favorite sugar free sweetner)\nYumm!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-27T22:00:51.333Z"
          },
          {
